  "problem": "Suppose we wish to calculate the Laplace transform \n\n$$\nL{t\\operatorname{cosh}\u20617t}.\n$$\n\n \nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below. You may make use of the following result:\n\n$$\nL{\\operatorname{cosh}\u2061\\omega t}=\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-{\\omega }^{2}},\\,s>\\omega .\n$$\n\nLet $f(t)=\\operatorname{cosh}\u20617t$ and $L{f(t)}=F(s).$ By the smoothness property of Laplace transforms,\n\n$$\nL{tf(t)}={{field-1}}.\n$$",
